<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portugal 3-yr bonds. [CORRECTED 11:23 GMT]</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portugal 3-yr bonds. [CORRECTED 11:23 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of three-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>    ISSUER: Republic of Portugal   MATURITY: 23 March 2000</p>
<p>    AMOUNT PLACED: 25 bln esc     COUPON: 5.375</p>
<p>(corrects coupon from 5.8953)</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.8959</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.90  LOWEST: 5.87</p>
<p>BIDS: 58.26 bln esc PAYMENT FREQUENCY:Annual</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 160.59 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
